; The counting loop of the Nexus M1 fixture. The counter is a `u64` that counts
; down by one each round, and the loop calls itself in tail position. When the
; counter is zero the loop makes an indirect tail call of `finish`, a function
; value that the other module defined.
(defn count (finish (fn () str) remaining u64) str
  visibility: @public
  (if
    (equatable.equal remaining 0u64)
    (finish)
    (count finish (u64.sub remaining 1u64))))
